   squash <hash2> <commit_message2>
   pick <hash3> <commit_message3>
   ```

4. Save and close the editor. You'll be prompted to enter a new commit message for the squashed commits.

5. Enter the new commit message and save.

6. Finish the rebase:
   ```bash
   git rebase --continue
   ```

7. Push the changes (force push might be needed if remote is already updated):
   ```bash
   git push origin <branch> --force
